{"number": 187, "text": "           Key\n\n\n            1 a-1, b-2         2 a-1, b2          3 a-2, b-1         4  a-1,b2\n\n           1  A: Id like a salad please.\n              B: A mixed salad or a Greek salad?\n                 What’s the difference?\n              A:\n                 Well, a mixed salad has tuna and a Greek salad has cheese.\n              B:\n\n           2 A:  I’d like to stay two nights please.\n             A:\n              B: Do you want full board or half board?\n             A:  What’s the difference?\n             B:  Full board includes all meals and half board includes just breakfast and dinner.\n\n           3  A: We'd like a room for two please.\n             A:\n                 Would you like standard or deluxe?\n             B:\n                 What’s the difference?\n             A:\n                Standard has a mountain view and  deluxe has a sea view.\n             B:\n\n\n   52.2\n           1 a-2, b-1          2 a-2, b-1\n\n   52.3\n           1 b-a           2 a-b          3  ba\n\n\n   53.1\n           1b              2b             3b              4a\n\n\n   53.2\n           1 A: No, the bathroom!\n           2 A: No, he’s retired!\n           3 A: No, a bookshelf.\n           4 A: No, I said impossible!\n           5 A: No, downstairs!\n\n   54.A\n           If a person who has a bad quality accuses you of having that same bad quality, you can reply\n           ‘Look who’s talking!’\n           If somebody tell you their plan, and the plan is very unlikely to succeed, you can reply “You’ll\n           be lucky!”\n\n   54.1\n           1                 2                 3\n\n           The meaning  of the expressions in this exercise is:\n           You must  be joking. — If someone makes a suggestion and you think it is a very bad idea, you\n           can say this.\n           Chance  would be a fine thing. If someone is telling you about something you would like to do\n           if you had the opportunity, you can say this.\n           Go  for it! - When someone is about to start a performance, you can encourage them by saying\n           this.\n           Give me a break. — If you achieve something in difficult circumstances and someone nevertheless\n           complains about it, you can say this.\n\n   54.2\n           1a-Who?       BS                            3    Yes?\n             b-Who?                                      b - Yes.\n           2 a—What?                                   4a—When?\n             b-What!     Ba                              b-When?\n\n\n  186\n              English Pronunciation in Use", "char_count": 2529, "mean_conf": 91.19, "word_count": 337, "words": [{"text": "52.2", "x0": 71, "y0": 1051, "x1": 177, "y1": 1091, "conf": 94, "bold": false}, {"text": "52.3", "x0": 71, "y0": 1168, "x1": 177, "y1": 1208, "conf": 95, "bold": false}, {"text": "53.1", "x0": 71, "y0": 1284, "x1": 169, "y1": 1323, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "53.2", "x0": 71, "y0": 1398, "x1": 175, "y1": 1438, "conf": 87, "bold": false}, {"text": "54.A", "x0": 66, "y0": 1716, "x1": 178, "y1": 1757, "conf": 90, "bold": false}, {"text": "54.1", "x0": 69, "y0": 2024, "x1": 167, "y1": 2062, "conf": 95, "bold": false}, {"text": "54.2", "x0": 66, "y0": 2721, "x1": 172, "y1": 2760, "conf": 91, "bold": false}, {"text": "186", "x0": 45, "y0": 3015, "x1": 111, "y1": 3049, "conf": 96, "bold": true}, {"text": "Key", "x0": 240, "y0": 4, "x1": 293, "y1": 42, "conf": 97, "bold": false}, {"text": "1", "x0": 242, "y0": 133, "x1": 259, "y1": 166, "conf": 89, "bold": false}, {"text": "a-1,", "x0": 286, "y0": 133, "x1": 364, "y1": 174, "conf": 87, "bold": false}, {"text": "b-2", "x0": 380, "y0": 130, "x1": 450, "y1": 166, "conf": 78, "bold": false}, {"text": "2", "x0": 645, "y0": 131, "x1": 668, "y1": 166, "conf": 90, "bold": false}, {"text": "a-1,", "x0": 692, "y0": 132, "x1": 771, "y1": 174, "conf": 89, "bold": false}, {"text": "b2", "x0": 786, "y0": 129, "x1": 856, "y1": 166, "